translate english day2_nightmare_836cb5fe:



    voice "voice/olya/2day/43 Tolko pust.ogg"
    Oly "I just want it to leave!"


translate english day2_nightmare_8c9ce15c:



    voice "voice/olya/2day/44 Pls.ogg"
    Oly "Please...!"


translate english day2_nightmare_9493d8c7:


    "The moonlight suddenly disappeared and the room descended into darkness. We couldn't see the burning eye anymore."


translate english day2_nightmare_60783264:


    "I swallowed the stingy lump that was stuck in my throat."


translate english day2_nightmare_87ce9218:


    "I stepped toward the curtains, entranced by the call of this disfigured guest"


translate english day2_nightmare_19c692ba:


    "Olya was standing behind me, mumbling: \"I'll be good, I'll be good, I'll be good!\""


translate english day2_nightmare_36cbc57e:


    "The bleak window was creeping closer. Curtains rustled."


translate english day2_nightmare_4dd91d3d:


    "I reached out to move them aside, so I could look my fear in the eye."


translate english day2_nightmare_8c15bcf2:


    "At that moment, I heard noise coming from our parents' bedroom."


translate english day2_nightmare_67c78d98:


    "Without thinking, I pulled the curtain to the side in one swing."


translate english day2_nightmare_4bb628cf:


    "Nothing."


translate english day2_nightmare_e92e7cf6:


    "Though, there was something shining on the ledge, among the scattered feathers."


translate english day2_nightmare_eaa01684:


    "My glasses."


translate english day2_nightmare_be6ab821:


    "The ones that Semyon took from me"


translate english day2_nightmare_e7909e93:


    "How did they get here...?"


translate english day2_nightmare_e88263aa:


    "Was that a gift from the gurgling night? Did that owl really bring them here?"


translate english day2_nightmare_366e9cd3:


    "I looked at the front yard, at the foreboding clearing, at the toothy forest."


translate english day2_nightmare_fc1cc08c:


    "Not a soul. Not a trace of our late night guest."


translate english day2_nightmare_c4fd22f0:


    "Only the old lamppost, dreaming like a lone watchman among the snowy desert."


translate english day2_nightmare_e3d48c2e:


    "The dry window frame creaked."


translate english day2_nightmare_d1ac9215:


    "I tore away the insulating tape and the {u}stipes of glued newspapers{/u}."


translate english day2_nightmare_46c562d6:


    "Opened the window with big trouble."


translate english day2_nightmare_74e37d7d:


    "Frost pinned me with its little needles. The paintings on my walls moved from the draft."


translate english day2_nightmare_13dba34e:


    "I touched my glasses, sure they would melt in my hands."


translate english day2_nightmare_dc860464:


    "But they were real."


translate english day2_nightmare_32f6824d:


    "My brain was scrambling for an explanation. Semyon and his gang just pulled a prank on me, that was it."


translate english day2_nightmare_9c797ad5:


    "That's it..."


translate english day2_nightmare_720c0ba4:


    "A smooth white blanket was glittering under the street lamp just outside our yard."


translate english day2_nightmare_b99940ae:


    "If anybody was to get close to the house, to climb the pipe to the ledge of my window, they would surely leave footprints."


translate english day2_nightmare_d910f327:


    "But there were none."


translate english day2_nightmare_cf3dd397:


    "I cautiously took my glasses."


translate english day2_nightmare_47d9aa6c:


    "My wrist was still intact."


translate english day2_nightmare_54bddbb1:


    "Nobody pulled me into the darkness, full of restless writhing."


translate english day2_nightmare_88a04769:



    voice "voice/karina/2day/95 Vy pochemy.ogg"
    Mam "Why aren't you in bed?!"


translate english day2_nightmare_492e8f8a:


